{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>מתם.</b> Men. Regarding the spoil of Sihon it is said בָּזַזְנוּ לָנוּ — a term of spoil, for it was precious to them and each man plundered for himself. But when they came to the spoil of Og, they were already sated and full, and it was contemptible in their eyes — they would tear and fling aside cattle and garments, taking only silver and gold. Therefore regarding it is said בַּזֹּנוּ לָנוּ — a term of בִּזָּיוֹן. Thus is it expounded in Sifrei, in the parashah of וַיֵּשֶׁב יִשְׂרָאֵל בַּשִּׁטִּים."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:45.389631896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}